# Strategy input → source archive (mandatory verbatim capture)

**SSOT:** [source-archive/statecraft/README.md](../../source-archive/statecraft/README.md) · [NOTEBOOK-PREFERENCES.md](../../codex/NOTEBOOK-PREFERENCES.md) · [RAW-INPUT-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/RAW-INPUT-DEPRECATED.md) · [statecraft-source-intake SKILL](../../.cursor/skills/statecraft-source-intake/SKILL.md)

**Deprecated:** `codex/raw-input/`, `codex/years/*/raw-input/`, and compat `docs/.../strategy-notebook/raw-input/` — do not write new captures there. See [RAW-INPUT-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/RAW-INPUT-DEPRECATED.md).

**Capture types:** When material is clearly **essay** (Substack, long web), **transcript** (YouTube, podcast), **social** (X, Locals, threads), or **wire / institutional PDF**, read the **source-intake** family table before choosing **`kind:`**, **`source_form:`**, and inbox-stub shape — do not default blindly to **`paste-bundle`** / **`mixed`** without checking that calibration.

## When this applies

Treat as **strategy input** when **any** of the following is true:

- The operator says **strategy input** (or obvious variants: **strategy input crooke**, **ingest this**, **notebook ingest**, **capture this for strategy**) **and** supplies or points at **external source material**.
- **Same intent without the exact phrase:** in **`docs/skill-work/work-strategy/`**, **`codex/`**, or clear **work-strategy** lane work, the operator pastes **full or substantial verbatim** (article, essay, statement, long excerpt) **with** a **URL** or **identifiable publication date/title**, expecting analysis — **not** a one-line headline-only prompt.

**Out of scope:** casual links with no paste and no request to retain text; pure **PLAN** / hypothesis threads where the operator declined disk writes; **Record** surfaces (`*`) — different pipeline.

## Required assistant behavior

1. **Land** via **`source-intake`** to  
   `source-archive/statecraft/<pub_date>/source-<slug>.md`  
   using the sidecar recipe in [statecraft-source-intake SKILL](../../.cursor/skills/statecraft-source-intake/SKILL.md) § Default execution order (`header.md` + body sidecar(s) + `land_statecraft_source_body.py`). **`pub_date`** = source publication day; optional **`ingest_date`** in YAML when useful; **`source_url`** when known.

2. **Filename:** always **`source-`** prefix — e.g. `source-crooke-<short-slug>.md` under the dated day folder — not legacy `substack-*` / `youtube-*` / `transcript-*` notebook names.

3. **Body:** **verbatim** operator-supplied text (or text fetched only if the operator clearly authorized fetch). **Do not** substitute synthesis for verbatim in the archive file.

4. **Same turn:** After the land (or in one batched edit), **then** deliver digest, tiers, seams, or **`days.md`** synthesis — notebook layers remain **synthesis + links**, not full mirrors.

5. **Optional:** Add a **short stub** to [`daily-strategy-inbox.md`](../../codex/daily-strategy-inbox.md) pointing at the **archive path** when the operator uses the inbox as a registry.

## If publication date is unknown

Use **`source-archive/statecraft/_aired-pending/`** until **`pub_date`** is pinned; then land under **`source-archive/statecraft/YYYY-MM-DD/`**.

## Do not

- Skip **source-archive** land because the reply already contains a good summary.
- Write new verbatim captures to **`codex/raw-input/`** or **`docs/.../strategy-notebook/raw-input/`**.
- Put **full source mirrors** only in **`chapters/…/days.md`** — violates NOTEBOOK-PREFERENCES (**notebook ≠ verbatim SSOT**).
- Synthesize or interpret **into** the archive capture — route interpretation to `statecraft/`, codex pages, or chat.
